            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0139" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/406: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-07-09T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1924—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>226. L–101, or Logan. Your L–189, July 8.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>The Department concurs in recommendation in paragraph 4 your telegram, and
                        presentation of note will be withheld until further advices from you.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>The Department will appreciate your comment on desirability of obtaining
                        from MacDonald through Kellogg before convening of London Conference
                        recognition of principle of American participation in payments looked to by
                        Dawes Plan in compensation of claims of this Government and of American
                        nationals, with understanding that details of participation be subject of
                        negotiation at time when the question of distribution will be
                        considered.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
